# Architecture Conventions

## Overall Policy

This engine adopts a hybrid **ECS x MVVM** architecture. Game logic (ECS) and UI (MVVM) are loosely coupled via message passing (event queues), without direct references.

## ECS (Entity Component System)

### Basic Rules

- Manage all game objects (3D models, Live2D characters, sprites, sound sources) as **Entity**.
- **Component** stores data only; no logic.
- **System** contains logic only; no state.
- Declare inter-system dependencies explicitly and control execution order.

### Component Design

```rust
// ✅ Data-only component
pub struct Transform {
    pub position: Vec3,
    pub rotation: Quat,
    pub scale: Vec3,
}

// ❌ Do not put logic in component methods
// -> Put logic in systems
```

### System Design

- Each system has a single responsibility (1 system = 1 concern).
- Defer side effects using the Command pattern.
- Keep queries minimal, targeting only required components.

## MVVM (UI Architecture)

### Layer Structure

| Layer | Responsibility | Technology |
|----------|------|------|
| **View** | UI node rendering/layout | Taffy (Flexbox), Filament rendering |
| **ViewModel** | UI state and `Signal<T>` management | Signal-driven reactive model |
| **Model** | ECS game data | Component / Resource |

### Communication Flow

#### UI -> ECS (Command Queue)

```text
View -> ViewModel -> Command -> mpsc::channel -> ECS System
```

- ViewModel translates user actions into a `Command` enum.
- Send commands via channel to ECS input-handling systems.
- ECS processes them safely in the next frame.

#### ECS -> UI (Signal Update)

```text
ECS component change detection -> ViewModel (Signal<T> update) -> View re-render
```

- UI sync systems detect component changes.
- Update corresponding ViewModel `Signal<T>`.
- Re-render only subscribed view nodes.

### Prohibited Patterns

- ❌ Direct ECS component read/write from View
- ❌ Direct View node manipulation from ECS systems
- ❌ Putting game logic into ViewModel

## Scene Trait

All game parts (ADV section, minigames, title screen, etc.) implement the `Scene` trait.

```rust
pub trait Scene: Send + Sync {
    /// Initialize scene (called after asset loading completes)
    fn on_enter(&mut self, ctx: &mut SceneContext);

    /// Per-frame update
    fn update(&mut self, ctx: &mut SceneContext, dt: f32) -> SceneTransition;

    /// Issue rendering commands
    fn render(&self, ctx: &RenderContext);

    /// Cleanup when leaving the scene
    fn on_exit(&mut self, ctx: &mut SceneContext);

    /// Asset list required by this scene
    fn required_assets(&self) -> Vec<AssetDescriptor>;
}
```

### Scene Transition Flow

1. Current scene `on_exit()` -> release resources
2. Fully purge assets (prevent leaks)
3. New scene `required_assets()` -> async load
4. After load, `on_enter()` -> initialize

## Plugin Pattern (Minigames)

- Build minigames as independent `Scene` trait implementations.
- Communicate with ADV part via message passing (`MiniGameResult` enum).
- Scope minigame-specific ECS components/systems in dedicated modules.
- Cleanup ECS on minigame end and return control to ADV part.

## Z-Order Rules

Use unified depth values for render layers.

| Layer | Z value | Description |
|----------|-------|------|
| Background | `10.0` | Background images, HDR environment map |
| 3D/Live2D | `0.0` to `5.0` | Characters/objects (ordered by draw order) |
| Characters | `-1.0` to `-5.0` | Foreground characters |
| UI/Text | `-10.0` | Topmost UI (orthographic camera, depth test off) |

## Multi-View Rendering

- **Game View (Layer 0)**: 3D space with PBR + IBL + Live2D (render-to-texture) + 2D sprites (quad).
- **UI View (Layer 1)**: Orthographic camera, depth test disabled, dedicated to UI/text rendering.

## Dual RNG

| Usage | Algorithm | Property |
|------|-------------|------|
| Visual effects (VisualRng) | Xoshiro256++ | Non-deterministic, fast |
| Logic (LogicRng) | ChaCha8 | Deterministic, replayable |

- Hand over LogicRng seeds across scene transitions in a chained manner.
- Include LogicRng seed state in save data.
